/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 32 968 [
[(Here we introduce the "append message to a [pointer] or [vpointer] object that adds)]
[(scalars to a window, and the [set] object that allows you to modify fields of scalars.)]
[(Our new, simpler [struct] object has five fields again but merely draws a rectangle)]
[(and one number for the color. Colors are in '999' form - see below about that.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 30 903 [
[(First an example appending an object: clicking the 'bang' clears the "data03" window)]
[(and then appends 20 new scalars to it. A [vpointer] object \050named with $0 in order to)]
[(make sure its name is unique to this patch\051 is pointed to an empty window \050the "clear")]
[(message empties it beforehand\051 using the "traverse" message and then sent 20 "append")]
[(messages. Each message specifies random values for the x, y, w, h, and c fields. This)]
[(causes a new scalar to be appended after the location the pointer is attached to.)]
[(Initially this is the head of the \050empty\051 window, and subsequently the vpointer is)]
[(updated so that each new scalar is then appended after the previous one.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 455 725 [
[(1: clear the window, \050Another good)]
[(reason to put your scalars in their)]
[(own window is so that you can clear)]
[(the window without clearing the rest)]
[(of the patch.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
